id: mind-reading
name: Mind Reading
uaType: magical
prerequisite: Insight Score of 6+, 2+ Skill Ranks in Clairvoyance
tpCost: 10
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCost: 0
requiresTarget: true
# "Target a Character who is not at Long Range" - within your Melee Range with Limited Range Reading - "and make a Clash
# (Cognitive) against them. If you win, increase your Dodge Rolls and the Dice Score of any Strike Roll made through the
# Parry effect of the Defend Maneuver against that Opponent by 1(T) until the end of your next turn" - the Mind Read mark
# on them, on your clock, read where those rolls are made (chat.mjs mindReadBonus). What you learn is the ARC's word.
mindReading: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  A Clash (Cognitive) at a Character not at Long Range: won, Dodge and Parry against them 1(T) higher until the end of your
  next turn, and what they know that you seek, as far as the ARC allows.
text: >
  Mind Reading: You are able to touch a target and read their mind, giving you a glimpse at their thoughts, and
  potentially aiding you in defending against them.
  –Ability Type: Magical
  –Prerequisites: Insight Score of 6+, 2+ Skill Ranks in Clairvoyance
  –TP Cost: 10
  –KP Cost: N/A
  –Maneuver Type: Standard
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –Minions: N/A
  –Passive Bonus: You gain access to the Instant Understanding Adventuring Maneuver.
  –Effect: Target a Character who is not at Long Range and make a Clash (Cognitive) against them. If you win, increase
  your Dodge Rolls and the Dice Score of any Strike Roll made through the Parry effect of the Defend Maneuver against that
  Opponent by 1(T) until the end of your next turn. Additionally, you may learn any piece of information they know that
  you are searching for. The amount of information you gain is limited by your ARC, some information may be repressed or
  Characters may have some unnatural resistance against this ability.

---

# The Passive Bonus waits on the Instant Understanding Adventuring Maneuver, which is not in this system yet.
